    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20805" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράκαι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span>, αἱ, Lat.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>braccae, breeches, trews, worn by the Gauls</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.30
			</span></i> (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράκες</span></b> 
				(sic)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">: ἀναξυρίδες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>):—
				Dim.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βράκια</span></b> , τά, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1082
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGiss.</u>
				80.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1406.23
			</span></i> (Edict. <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.
			</span></i>, Asine):— hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρακάριος</span></b> , ὁ,
				<i>breeches-maker</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1341
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>:— but <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρακαρίαι</span></b> , αἱ,
				<i>breeches,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PGiss.
				90.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>.</div>
